[interviewer · EXHIBIT · 5:29] Walk me through the translation from that 28% to the margin. COGS was 42% of revenue two years ago, and 28% is a share of COGS. You asked about that — Raw coffee bean costs are up 40% over the past two years. How many points of revenue does it represent?

[candidate · 6:47] Let me do it in points of revenue. Old COGS was 42 points. Beans were 25% of that, so 10.5 points, and other inputs 75%, so 31.5 points.

Beans up 40%: 10.5 × 1.4 = 14.7, so +4.2 points.
Other inputs up 37.5%: 31.5 × 1.375 = 43.3, so +11.8 points.

Total new COGS = 14.7 + 43.3 = 58 points, which matches the 58% you gave me. So the increase is about 16 points of revenue, with roughly 12 from other inputs and 4 from beans.

That 16 plus the 2 points of overhead is about 18, which is the whole 24% to 6% drop.
